WEBVTT

00:00:12.450 --> 00:00:18.600
Do you hear?  Hooves beating

00:00:25.430 --> 00:00:30.750
A carriage goes through the gentle hills

00:00:33.050 --> 00:00:37.980
Someone comes to pick me up

00:00:39.070 --> 00:00:45.950
And takes me

00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:49.900
To the avenue with white flowers

00:00:52.620 --> 00:00:58.050
To the home of wind

00:00:58.950 --> 00:01:02.400
He takes me

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:08.900
I'm sure

00:01:47.900 --> 00:01:50.230
It looks like a beautiful day again.

00:01:54.100 --> 00:01:56.040
Good morning, Diana!

00:02:04.750 --> 00:02:08.400
Diana! Please listen to me!

00:02:08.520 --> 00:02:12.660
Oh, didn't you say yesterday that
our friendship was over?

00:02:12.890 --> 00:02:15.370
So I don't want to talk with you.

00:02:15.370 --> 00:02:19.000
That's why I'm apologizing to you.

00:02:19.860 --> 00:02:21.620
Please forgive me!

00:02:21.620 --> 00:02:24.720
Or else my last letter to you
was meaningless.

00:02:25.370 --> 00:02:26.610
What last letter?

00:02:26.610 --> 00:02:28.220
My last letter to you.

00:02:28.220 --> 00:02:31.440
I was dying for eating a poisoned apple.

00:02:33.260 --> 00:02:38.560
Later on, I found out the apple
wasn't poisoned after all

00:02:38.560 --> 00:02:41.410
but I really wrote you a last letter.

00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:43.890
That is so like you, Anne.

00:02:44.230 --> 00:02:45.750
Alright, I forgive you.

00:02:45.970 --> 00:02:48.430
I can't be angry with
someone who has died.

00:02:49.020 --> 00:02:49.780
Thank goodness!

00:02:49.900 --> 00:02:52.240
Then tell me what you wanted to say.

00:02:52.240 --> 00:02:53.110
All right.

00:02:58.390 --> 00:03:01.290
Today I have great news.

00:03:01.400 --> 00:03:03.960
I'm going to join the Queen's class.

00:03:03.960 --> 00:03:05.600
Oh my! Really, Anne?

00:03:05.600 --> 00:03:09.300
Yes. Yesterday, Miss Stacy
came to talk about it

00:03:09.300 --> 00:03:13.190
and Marilla and Matthew
agreed to let me go.

00:03:13.710 --> 00:03:17.680
If I can get into Queen's,
I'll be able to become a teacher in the future.

00:03:17.930 --> 00:03:19.910
But of course I'll have to pass
the entrance exam first.

00:03:19.910 --> 00:03:21.280
I'm so glad for you, Anne.

00:03:21.550 --> 00:03:24.680
You're a model pupil so
you'll definitely make it.

00:03:25.130 --> 00:03:26.260
Thank you, Diana.

00:03:26.810 --> 00:03:29.370
I'll study hard for it.

00:03:29.650 --> 00:03:33.360
I want to go with you to the Queen's
Academy and study all sort of things.

00:03:33.650 --> 00:03:36.200
I won't even be afraid of geometry.

00:03:36.890 --> 00:03:39.840
Both my parents were teachers

00:03:39.840 --> 00:03:43.340
so I always dreamed of
becoming a teacher too.

00:03:43.340 --> 00:03:48.640
Although I'm living right now at
Green Gables, I'm still an orphan.

00:03:48.760 --> 00:03:52.830
So I couldn't bring myself to say
that I wanted to go to Queen's Academy.

00:03:53.840 --> 00:03:58.830
But Matthew and Marilla told me that
from the moment they decided to adopt me,

00:03:59.220 --> 00:04:04.110
they resolved they would do the best they
could for me and give me a good education.

00:04:04.720 --> 00:04:08.830
Oh, you can't imagine how grateful
I am to Marilla and Matthew.

00:04:09.310 --> 00:04:12.740
I don't even feel the cold this morning,

00:04:12.960 --> 00:04:15.310
because I feel so happy.

00:04:15.900 --> 00:04:17.150
What's the matter, Diana?

00:04:18.360 --> 00:04:21.000
Are you still angry about yesterday?

00:04:21.380 --> 00:04:22.780
It's not that.

00:04:23.020 --> 00:04:24.590
That's good...

00:04:25.500 --> 00:04:27.400
I had a dream.

00:04:28.250 --> 00:04:31.850
I dreamt that both of us made it to Queen's.

00:04:32.020 --> 00:04:36.160
It was only a dream but my heart
started pounding madly.

00:04:36.420 --> 00:04:37.190
Anne.

00:04:37.190 --> 00:04:38.220
Yes?

00:04:40.210 --> 00:04:42.290
I can't go to Queen's Academy.

00:04:54.950 --> 00:04:58.140
Diana, is what you said before true?

00:04:58.290 --> 00:04:59.490
Yes.

00:04:59.490 --> 00:05:00.600
Why?

00:05:01.250 --> 00:05:04.740
Miss Stacy was in your
house yesterday, wasn't she?

00:05:04.830 --> 00:05:05.450
Yes.

00:05:05.630 --> 00:05:07.070
Then, why?

00:05:09.260 --> 00:05:11.290
Anne Shirley. Is something wrong?

00:05:20.870 --> 00:05:21.700
Diana,

00:05:21.920 --> 00:05:24.050
please tell me why you're
not going to Queen's Academy.

00:05:24.970 --> 00:05:28.830
I've always thought
that we would study together.

00:05:29.600 --> 00:05:35.510
When we were at the exposition, didn't
you said that you were born for the city's life?

00:05:35.670 --> 00:05:36.620
That's why, I...

00:05:36.620 --> 00:05:37.190
Anne,

00:05:37.280 --> 00:05:38.530
I don't want to talk about it anymore.

00:05:38.530 --> 00:05:39.800
No, we have to.

00:05:39.920 --> 00:05:42.690
If you're not going,
then I'm not going too.

00:05:43.230 --> 00:05:45.780
My mother and father
were the ones who decided.

00:05:45.880 --> 00:05:47.390
They won't let me go.

00:05:47.960 --> 00:05:50.330
So please forget about it.

00:05:50.800 --> 00:05:52.150
How can that be?

00:05:52.770 --> 00:05:55.010
But Diana, how do you feel about it?

00:05:55.210 --> 00:05:56.500
Don't you want to go to Queen's?

00:05:56.880 --> 00:05:59.510
Jane, Ruby and Josie are going.

00:05:59.940 --> 00:06:03.140
I think that it would
be fun to study with them.

00:06:03.300 --> 00:06:04.230
That's right.

00:06:04.520 --> 00:06:08.760
If even I can go, then
there's no reason why you can't.

00:06:09.170 --> 00:06:10.980
That may be truth, but...

00:06:11.080 --> 00:06:13.930
Then speak to your parents about it.

00:06:14.210 --> 00:06:14.960
Yes...

00:06:15.500 --> 00:06:16.300
But...

00:06:16.570 --> 00:06:18.360
Let me accompany you.

00:06:18.790 --> 00:06:20.430
I'm sure we'll be able to convince them.

00:06:20.800 --> 00:06:22.530
There is no need. I'll speak to them myself.

00:06:22.630 --> 00:06:23.370
Really?

00:06:23.630 --> 00:06:24.330
Yes...

00:06:24.870 --> 00:06:26.460
Make sure you make them understand.

00:06:26.750 --> 00:06:27.760
Alright, Anne.

00:06:27.960 --> 00:06:29.580
So please don't talk more about it.

00:06:29.680 --> 00:06:30.520
Goodbye.

00:06:37.670 --> 00:06:42.180
I never expected Diana not to be
allowed to get into Queens.

00:06:42.410 --> 00:06:44.740
And Diana is also to be blamed.

00:06:44.740 --> 00:06:49.380
She gave up right away instead
of talking with her parents.

00:06:49.780 --> 00:06:50.220
Anne,

00:06:50.290 --> 00:06:55.000
the problem is you think you're always right.

00:06:55.250 --> 00:06:59.410
Mr. Barry must have his
reasons to decide that about Diana.

00:06:59.620 --> 00:07:01.850
You shouldn't have meddled.

00:07:02.050 --> 00:07:03.520
But it's too much.

00:07:03.600 --> 00:07:05.520
They didn't even ask Diana about it.

00:07:06.430 --> 00:07:09.180
And you think you understand Diana?

00:07:09.670 --> 00:07:14.110
Does she really want to
become a teacher just like you do?

00:07:15.160 --> 00:07:17.390
That is the reason
why you want to go to Queen's.

00:07:17.950 --> 00:07:25.530
You probably were so forceful
that Diana couldn't speak her mind.

00:07:26.070 --> 00:07:30.340
She has the right
to seek the lifestyle she desires.

00:07:39.000 --> 00:07:44.680
I've always thought it would be
great to prepare for exams with Diana.

00:07:45.100 --> 00:07:49.290
And I always believed that
Diana felt the same way too.

00:07:51.240 --> 00:07:56.690
But Anne, we can't force
others to live the way we want them to.

00:08:29.650 --> 00:08:31.170
Good morning, Diana!

00:08:34.970 --> 00:08:35.720
Anne,

00:08:35.990 --> 00:08:37.980
forget about
what we spoke about yesterday.

00:08:38.060 --> 00:08:38.900
I...

00:08:39.030 --> 00:08:40.040
It's not that!

00:08:40.300 --> 00:08:42.050
Anyway, come down.

00:08:47.710 --> 00:08:49.990
I've always felt that

00:08:50.260 --> 00:08:56.800
we should do everything together, like going
to Queen's and not getting married.

00:08:57.390 --> 00:09:01.760
And I forgot about your opinion.

00:09:02.940 --> 00:09:04.350
But I was wrong.

00:09:04.440 --> 00:09:11.310
Even if we end up in different paths,
true friends should still support each other.

00:09:12.500 --> 00:09:13.550
Anne...

00:09:13.830 --> 00:09:16.420
Marilla made me realize that yesterday.

00:09:16.810 --> 00:09:21.020
We can be good friends even if we
don't attend school together.

00:09:21.330 --> 00:09:26.430
You'll make a wonderful wife
no matter who you marry.

00:09:26.490 --> 00:09:27.910
A-Anne...!

00:09:29.710 --> 00:09:33.160
Diana, forgive me for making you feel so bad,

00:09:33.160 --> 00:09:40.190
and let us renew our promise in
the same place we did before.

00:09:43.760 --> 00:09:45.500
Thank you, Diana.

00:09:57.150 --> 00:10:02.630
Even if we're separated,
so long as time goes by,

00:10:02.800 --> 00:10:06.830
I solemnly swear to be faithful to
my bosom friend, Diana Barry

00:10:06.900 --> 00:10:08.340
as long as the sun and moon shall endure.

00:10:09.130 --> 00:10:14.570
Even if we're separated,
so long as time goes by,

00:10:14.700 --> 00:10:18.600
I solemnly swear to be faithful to
my bosom friend, Anne Shirley

00:10:18.610 --> 00:10:20.230
as long as the sun and moon shall endure.

00:10:53.640 --> 00:10:56.290
Never, since the night on which
Minnie May had the croup,

00:10:56.800 --> 00:10:59.920
had Anne and Diana
been separated in anything.

00:11:00.390 --> 00:11:03.320
Diana won't be joining the Queen's class.

00:11:03.900 --> 00:11:09.580
From now on they will be
moving on in life in different directions.

00:11:12.430 --> 00:11:15.640
The Queen's class
was organized in due time.

00:11:15.780 --> 00:11:16.920
Gilbert Blythe,

00:11:16.920 --> 00:11:17.840
Anne Shirley,

00:11:17.970 --> 00:11:19.040
Ruby Gillis,

00:11:19.250 --> 00:11:20.470
Jane Andrews,

00:11:20.720 --> 00:11:21.780
Josie Pye,

00:11:21.780 --> 00:11:22.960
Charlie Sloane,

00:11:23.040 --> 00:11:26.420
and Moody Spurgeon MacPherson joined it.

00:11:26.670 --> 00:11:31.890
As Anne had expected,
Diana's name was not included.

00:11:32.340 --> 00:11:36.780
The students I just called
please stay in here for extra lessons.

00:11:36.860 --> 00:11:39.660
As for the rest, we'll see you tomorrow.

00:11:41.930 --> 00:11:42.920
Anne.

00:11:50.530 --> 00:11:51.880
Work hard, Anne.

00:11:53.020 --> 00:11:54.160
Diana...

00:12:09.450 --> 00:12:11.800
Dearest Anne Shirley,

00:12:12.280 --> 00:12:20.290
as you have understood, it's not just because
of my parents that I'm not going to Queen's.

00:12:20.850 --> 00:12:25.910
I don't enjoy studying like you
do and I don't wish to become a teacher.

00:12:26.440 --> 00:12:30.120
I should've told you this long ago.

00:12:31.460 --> 00:12:34.400
You will forgive me for not
having told you the truth, won't you?

00:12:36.070 --> 00:12:41.490
But my heart will always be with you.

00:12:42.050 --> 00:12:44.400
Even if I don't go to Queen's,

00:12:44.850 --> 00:12:48.860
we must remain good friends forever.

00:12:49.370 --> 00:12:51.350
Please work hard on my behalf

00:12:51.600 --> 00:12:53.550
and realize your dream as soon as possible.

00:12:54.390 --> 00:12:57.480
From your bosom friend, Diana Barry.

00:12:58.550 --> 00:12:59.470
Diana...

00:13:02.150 --> 00:13:03.260
What's the matter, Anne?

00:13:06.510 --> 00:13:07.850
It's nothing, Ruby.

00:13:14.620 --> 00:13:15.260
Anne,

00:13:15.550 --> 00:13:18.040
are you still thinking about Diana?

00:13:18.340 --> 00:13:21.430
You're not going to part forever.

00:13:21.440 --> 00:13:22.820
Marilla,

00:13:23.270 --> 00:13:26.610
I wish to support
Diana's decision wholeheartedly.

00:13:27.200 --> 00:13:32.620
But when I saw Diana go out alone,
I had the urge to go after her.

00:13:33.060 --> 00:13:38.870
I really felt that I had
tasted the bitterness of death.

00:13:39.660 --> 00:13:40.680
My goodness,

00:13:40.730 --> 00:13:43.040
don't exaggerate.

00:13:43.040 --> 00:13:47.490
It's another year until you go to Queen's.

00:13:47.490 --> 00:13:50.300
You can have fun with Diana in the meantime.

00:13:51.350 --> 00:13:57.050
As Mrs. Lynde says, we can't have things
perfect in this imperfect world.

00:13:57.550 --> 00:14:02.120
I just have to accept that we
have to go on different ways.

00:14:04.500 --> 00:14:09.560
But I feel so lonely to have
to part with Diana.

00:14:20.340 --> 00:14:24.460
It's been two months since the
extra lessons for Queen's started.

00:14:26.720 --> 00:14:33.620
Except for Josie Pye refusing to sit with Anne,
everything went smoothly for the students.

00:14:34.640 --> 00:14:38.850
Now, please try to solve this problem.
This one is a little hard.

00:14:47.330 --> 00:14:49.620
Looks like you're all in trouble.

00:14:49.620 --> 00:14:50.840
Does anyone know the answer?

00:14:50.960 --> 00:14:51.320
Me!

00:14:52.430 --> 00:14:52.900
Me!

00:14:53.420 --> 00:14:57.090
Then Anne and Gilbert, please
write your answers on the board.

00:14:58.060 --> 00:15:00.740
The rest of you, please keep trying.

00:15:01.370 --> 00:15:05.250
There was open rivalry
between Gilbert and Anne now.

00:15:05.990 --> 00:15:09.850
Previously the
rivalry had been rather onesided,

00:15:10.300 --> 00:15:12.700
but there was no
longer any doubt that Gilbert

00:15:12.820 --> 00:15:16.850
was as determined
to be first in class as Anne was.

00:15:18.880 --> 00:15:22.850
To Anne, Gilbert was
a foeman worthy of her steel.

00:15:26.810 --> 00:15:31.380
Marilla, everyone at the
Queen's class has great ambitions.

00:15:31.700 --> 00:15:35.090
Jane and Ruby
are just going to study to be teachers.

00:15:35.380 --> 00:15:38.210
That is the height of their ambition.

00:15:38.500 --> 00:15:41.050
I will only teach for
two years after I get through,

00:15:41.050 --> 00:15:42.700
and then I intend to be married.

00:15:42.940 --> 00:15:46.100
I will devote my whole life to teaching,

00:15:46.460 --> 00:15:48.490
and I will never, never marry!

00:15:48.820 --> 00:15:51.470
Because you are paid a salary for teaching,

00:15:51.700 --> 00:15:54.190
but a husband won't pay you anything.

00:15:54.610 --> 00:15:55.980
Jane says

00:15:56.380 --> 00:15:57.940
a husband won't pay you anything,

00:15:58.030 --> 00:16:02.510
and growls if you ask for
a share in the egg and butter money.

00:16:03.000 --> 00:16:06.040
I expect Jane speaks
from mournful experience.

00:16:06.190 --> 00:16:08.340
Is that so?

00:16:08.800 --> 00:16:13.360
Mrs. Lynde says that
Jane's father is a perfect old crank,

00:16:13.360 --> 00:16:14.940
and meaner than second skimmings.

00:16:15.550 --> 00:16:17.130
And Josie Pye says...

00:16:17.390 --> 00:16:21.160
I'm just going to college for education's sake,

00:16:21.550 --> 00:16:25.030
because I won't have to earn my own living.

00:16:25.460 --> 00:16:29.840
It is different with orphans who
are living on charity.

00:16:29.840 --> 00:16:34.590
She talks like all orphans
have to work to survive.

00:16:35.130 --> 00:16:36.330
Just ignore her.

00:16:36.330 --> 00:16:39.980
Orphan or not, everyone
have to work to survive.

00:16:40.070 --> 00:16:46.000
That's right, Anne.
Besides... you're no longer an orphan.

00:16:47.250 --> 00:16:48.370
Matthew!

00:16:48.920 --> 00:16:53.850
W-well now...
What about the other students?

00:16:54.120 --> 00:16:58.250
The boys are Moody Spurgeon,
Charlie and Gilbert.

00:16:58.630 --> 00:17:00.550
I'm going to be a minister.

00:17:00.840 --> 00:17:02.600
I know it's wicked of me,

00:17:02.600 --> 00:17:06.570
but the thought of Moody Spurgeon
being a minister makes me laugh.

00:17:06.950 --> 00:17:10.850
Because he doesn't look like one at all.

00:17:10.850 --> 00:17:15.390
But perhaps he will be more
intellectual looking when he grows up.

00:17:16.000 --> 00:17:17.650
And Charlie Sloane says...

00:17:17.860 --> 00:17:21.230
I'm going to go into politics
and be a member of Parliament.

00:17:21.360 --> 00:17:22.970
I'll strive for your welfare.

00:17:23.280 --> 00:17:24.380
But Marilla,

00:17:24.490 --> 00:17:27.580
Mrs. Lynde
says he'll never succeed at that,

00:17:27.740 --> 00:17:31.230
because the Sloanes are all honest people,

00:17:31.230 --> 00:17:35.080
and it's only rascals that
get on in politics nowadays.

00:17:35.710 --> 00:17:38.420
What is Gilbert Blythe going to be?

00:17:39.700 --> 00:17:43.840
I don't happen to know
what Gilbert Blythe's ambition in life is,

00:17:44.120 --> 00:17:46.390
if he has any.

00:17:49.240 --> 00:17:54.340
Since the day by the pond when Anne had
refused to listen to his plea for forgiveness,

00:17:54.440 --> 00:17:57.950
Gilbert Blythe, save for the determined rivalry,

00:17:58.090 --> 00:18:01.180
had evinced no recognition
whatever of the existence of Anne.

00:18:01.820 --> 00:18:04.200
He talked and jested with the other girls,

00:18:04.300 --> 00:18:07.820
exchanged books and puzzles with
them, discussed lessons and plans,

00:18:07.830 --> 00:18:10.380
sometimes walked home
with one or the other of them.

00:18:10.460 --> 00:18:12.420
But Anne he simply ignored.

00:18:16.630 --> 00:18:18.550
Anne didn't like that.

00:18:18.880 --> 00:18:24.860
It was in vain that she told herself with
a toss of her head that she did not care.

00:18:24.860 --> 00:18:28.190
Deep down in her feminine
little heart she did care,

00:18:28.190 --> 00:18:33.160
and if she had that chance of the
Lake of Shining Waters again

00:18:33.160 --> 00:18:35.230
she would answer very differently.

00:18:35.470 --> 00:18:41.100
But she determined to "shroud
her feelings in deepest oblivion,"

00:18:41.100 --> 00:18:47.400
and she did it so successfully that
no one suspected how she truly felt.

00:18:54.700 --> 00:18:56.340
Oh, you're back.

00:18:57.740 --> 00:19:00.640
It started to snow heavily all of a sudden.

00:19:00.730 --> 00:19:02.230
Will Anne be able to come back safely?

00:19:02.380 --> 00:19:03.860
Well now,

00:19:04.330 --> 00:19:07.400
maybe I should fetch her from school.

00:19:07.820 --> 00:19:12.310
They should end the extra lessons
earlier in a weather like this.

00:19:16.110 --> 00:19:18.720
Teacher, this is all the wood we've got.

00:19:18.980 --> 00:19:20.400
That's strange.

00:19:20.400 --> 00:19:23.090
There should've been
some delivered here this morning.

00:19:24.200 --> 00:19:25.290
Well, it's all right.

00:19:25.370 --> 00:19:26.600
Let's continue.

00:19:36.440 --> 00:19:38.160
Quiet, everyone.

00:19:38.280 --> 00:19:39.640
It's just snowing.

00:19:40.080 --> 00:19:42.170
Teacher, we should
go home as soon as possible.

00:19:42.500 --> 00:19:44.710
That's right.
We should go before it's too late!

00:19:44.840 --> 00:19:47.130
Teacher, if we go now it should be safe.

00:19:48.310 --> 00:19:49.300
Wait.

00:19:51.090 --> 00:19:52.380
Some of us live faraway.

00:19:52.650 --> 00:19:54.910
What would we do if the
snow gets heavy on our way?

00:19:55.150 --> 00:19:56.780
We'd better wait a while.

00:19:57.070 --> 00:19:58.540
But we're running out of firewood.

00:19:58.540 --> 00:20:01.380
If we have to,
we could use the tables and the chairs.

00:20:02.140 --> 00:20:05.760
Meanwhile, I think it would be safer to stay
here until someone comes to fetch us, teacher.

00:20:05.880 --> 00:20:07.680
That's right, we should wait.

00:20:07.680 --> 00:20:08.440
I think so too.

00:20:08.650 --> 00:20:12.600
Yes, I think that's the best thing to do.

00:20:12.600 --> 00:20:14.950
Well, let's continue the lessons.

00:20:14.950 --> 00:20:15.950
Yes!

00:20:23.000 --> 00:20:24.970
This is the last piece of wood.

00:20:26.300 --> 00:20:29.080
Don't cry Ruby. It's almost over.

00:20:29.080 --> 00:20:32.650
Almost over?
No one's coming to fetch us in this weather.

00:20:32.650 --> 00:20:34.100
We should stay here and wait.

00:20:34.100 --> 00:20:38.090
Come on, we should put our
coats on before we freeze.

00:20:38.090 --> 00:20:40.350
I don't want to freeze!

00:20:40.360 --> 00:20:41.610
Neither do I!

00:20:41.610 --> 00:20:43.940
Calm down!

00:20:44.360 --> 00:20:45.050
Teacher,

00:20:45.590 --> 00:20:50.320
I'll go to Mr. Andrews' house to ask
how long the snowstorm is expected to last.

00:20:50.730 --> 00:20:53.760
And If necessary,
I'll bring some food and firewood.

00:20:53.840 --> 00:20:55.470
No, that's too dangerous.

00:20:55.730 --> 00:20:57.220
His house it's not too far.

00:20:57.350 --> 00:20:58.510
I'll go too.

00:20:59.200 --> 00:21:01.290
Wait, let's think of something else.

00:21:01.530 --> 00:21:02.300
We'll be alright!

00:21:02.380 --> 00:21:03.330
We'll be back soon.

00:21:15.900 --> 00:21:17.020
Hang in there!

00:21:18.050 --> 00:21:19.130
I can't see anything!

00:21:28.540 --> 00:21:31.320
Even after exercising both lets, I'm still cold.

00:21:31.750 --> 00:21:33.260
I wonder if Gil and the others are alright?

00:21:33.340 --> 00:21:35.200
Gil is really reliable.

00:21:35.240 --> 00:21:37.850
Charlie and Moody have gone too.

00:21:37.850 --> 00:21:39.510
But it was Gil who decided.

00:21:39.830 --> 00:21:44.410
You want your name to be written in
the wall along with Gil's name, don't you?

00:21:46.760 --> 00:21:48.650
The water is almost frozen!

00:21:49.650 --> 00:21:50.070
Really?

00:21:50.070 --> 00:21:53.290
Come on, let's sing to warm up.

00:21:53.600 --> 00:21:56.630
We'll sing louder than the storm.

00:21:56.880 --> 00:21:58.190
Start!

00:22:23.620 --> 00:22:24.880
They're taking so long.

00:22:25.220 --> 00:22:27.290
Don't worry, they'll come back soon.

00:22:27.430 --> 00:22:30.720
What are we going to do
if they don't return?

00:22:30.730 --> 00:22:32.640
Ruby, calm down!

00:22:34.530 --> 00:22:36.070
We're doomed!

00:22:39.020 --> 00:22:40.270
Ruby Gillis!

00:22:43.030 --> 00:22:44.880
Are you all right, Ruby?

00:22:56.440 --> 00:22:59.030
Jane, did you hear something?

00:22:59.040 --> 00:23:00.830
It was the wind.

00:23:01.430 --> 00:23:02.790
No, it wasn't.

00:23:13.240 --> 00:23:14.350
It's Gilbert!

00:23:14.530 --> 00:23:16.000
They're back!

00:23:34.800 --> 00:23:35.890
Gilbert!

00:23:37.000 --> 00:23:38.680
Teacher, we can leave now!

00:23:39.110 --> 00:23:41.480
The storm will be lighter soon.

00:24:17.500 --> 00:24:21.060
Marilla is worried about Anne
getting exhausted studying for the exams

00:24:21.060 --> 00:24:23.730
and Anne is excited over
the coming summer holidays.

00:24:23.900 --> 00:24:26.550
Next episode of Anne of Green Gables:

00:24:26.800 --> 00:24:28.480
Longing for the Summer Holidays

00:24:28.700 --> 00:24:29.790
Please watch!
